cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, discuss, or build on DEP, please cite it as below."
title: "Project Hoopeo: Database-Enforced Privacy (DEP)"
abstract: >-
  A design for a database server in which privacy is part of the type system,
  the query semantics, and the execution engine. Protected values can be used
  for matching one value at a time but are never returned by ordinary queries;
  linking whole datasets and disclosing values are allowed only in functions
  declared LINKS and DISCLOSES, so every such place is reviewable and listed
  in the catalog.
